    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full suite is green \u2014 **56 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors**, BUILD SUCCESS.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `timezone` field on the owner response, derived from the owner's locality/region via the fixed region-to-timezone table.\n\nThree changes, following the existing `locality` pattern:\n\n1. **`util/Localities.java`** \u2014 added a `REGION_TIMEZONE` table (`NSW \u2192 Australia/Sydney`, `VIC \u2192 Australia/Melbourne`, `QLD \u2192 Australia/Brisbane`) and a `timezone(postcode, city)` method that resolves the region via the existing `region(postcode, city)` logic and looks up its IANA name (returns `null` for `UNKNOWN`/no known timezone).\n\n2. **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a MapStruct `@Mapping` wiring `OwnerDto.timezone` to `Localities.timezone(owner.getPostcode(), owner.getCity())`.\n\n3. **`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `timezone` string property to the Owner schema so the generated `OwnerDto` exposes it.\n\n`Cp42Tests` (which asserts `$.timezone == \"Australia/Sydney\"` for a Sydney/NSW owner) passes, and no existing tests regressed.",
